| `tools/round-69/packed-elf.py` | gate — R69-C1/C2/C3: supersession of the round-68 packed-ELF route (which stays byte-identical) — the arm seam `evaluate_carrier()` with 20 selftest cases including one arm-false case per arm; a typed preflight (exit 2 `unevaluable` for missing node/git/readelf/upx, an unusable `--work`, a packer version or sha256 mismatch) with the UPX 5.2.0 pin ENFORCED; per-carrier records naming name, format (readelf -h), packing_mode (`upx --best`) and pin; a third pinned carrier of kind shared-object (`/usr/lib/libz.so.1.3.2`); and `--check-receipt` for R69-C3 (target 3, every arm, every ceiling ratio <= 0.75, a shared-object carrier) | 0=met: carriers_matched 3 of 3, control_ok true, failing []; 1=not met: each false arm/clause named and the receipt still written; 2=could-not-evaluate: each typed `unevaluable` class above, carrier pin drift, REA package drift, unknown revision or bad argv | `python3 -I -B tools/round-69/packed-elf.py --selftest` — 20 cases, exit 0 on 2026-11-03; `--check-receipt` exit 0 on a synthetic in-bounds receipt and exit 1 with `libz: before_ceiling_ratio 0.9 > 0.75` on the loose-ceiling fixture | `.ufo/waves/round-69/l1/pre/` (base arms), `.ufo/waves/round-69/w1/` (wave evidence); scratch under $HYAKU_SCRATCH | UPX_SHA256_PIN, UPX_VERSION_PIN, the CARRIERS table (sha256, floors, stub ceilings) and REA_PKGJSON_SHA256 in the source, all enforced | --json-out receipt and --work scratch; every copy is rebuilt inside --work and deleted | kaidoku |
| `tools/round-69/mutation-check.py` | gate — R69-C1 calibration: applies the five 2026-11-03 route mutants (M1_identity, M2_recovery, M3_detected, M4_before, M5_control) to a git blob in scratch and runs only the instrument's `--selftest`; patch set r68 expects the five survivors at 13 cases, patch set r69 expects 0 survivors with each kill naming its declared arm-false case (`killed_wrong_case` is never a kill) | 0=expectation met; 1=missed, each survivor and wrong-case kill named; 2=could-not-evaluate (unknown revision, patch site absent or ambiguous, pristine selftest not green, refused --work, bad argv) | `mutation-check.py --validate <receipt>` checks a battery receipt's structural honesty (mutant rows, int rc, failed list, survivors consistent); controls reject an empty-record receipt | `.ufo/waves/round-69/l1/pre/c1-at-base.json` (5 survivors) and the landing receipt (0) | the PATCH_SETS table (each patch site and its expected arm-false case) in the source | --json-out receipt only; every mutant lives in scratch | kaidoku |
| `tools/round-69/contract-probe.py` | gate — R69-C2 operability: six black-box arms against the instrument under test — A1 a PATH without node, A2 an unwritable --work, A3 `--upx` a script reporting 5.1.0, A4 `--upx` a real upx plus one byte, A5 the receipt's carrier records re-derived from the pinned source bytes and the pack argv, A6 the receipt's enforced packer pins against the host packer | 0=all six arms pass; 1=arms failed, each named with its observation; 2=could-not-evaluate (unknown revision, missing host tool, bad argv) | `contract-probe.py --validate <receipt>` checks the arm rows, observations and the `arms_passed`/`failed` consistency | `.ufo/waves/round-69/l1/pre/c2-at-base.json` (0 of 6) and the landing probe receipt (6 of 6) | UPX path, PACKING_MODE and the six arm ids in the source; the instrument under test is named by --rev and --tool | --json-out receipt only; fixtures live in scratch | kaidoku |
| `tools/round-69/controls.py` | gate — the round's seven do-nothing/shortcut controls, scored with the same frozen counters: c1-do-nothing (r68 instrument + r68 patch set, 5 survivors), c1-constant-battery (rejected), c2-do-nothing (base instrument + base receipt, 0 of 6), c2-constant-probe (rejected), c3-do-nothing (r68 receipt, target 2), c3-synthetic-met (in-bounds receipt, met), c3-loose-ceiling (ratio 0.9, rejected) | 0=every control shows what it must show; 1=any control misses its expectation, named; 2=bad argv or a missing --work | `controls.py --root . --rev <base> --work <scratch> --json-out <receipt>` | `.ufo/waves/round-69/l1/pre/controls-at-base.json` | the four tool paths in TOOLS and BASE_RECEIPT in the source | --json-out receipt only; synthetic receipts and scratch fixtures | kaidoku |
